<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koga, Ibaraki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koga is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibaraki-prefecture">Ibaraki Prefecture</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto region</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, formerly in Shimousa province. In 1455 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-shigeuji">Ashikaga Shigeuji</a>, driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a>, made it his base, and his line ruled from there as the Koga kubo until the late 16th century. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a> it was a castle town and post station on the road north from Edo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koga-ibaraki.jpg" alt="Koga, Ibaraki" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Altomarina · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koga_city_hall_(Ibaraki).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
